From 9bd2fe32d2b8ff52ba250acbc345a250f3e2f724 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 03:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix review findings: cannibalization gate in classic flow,
 embeddings timeout + precedence

Addresses two code-review findings + the embeddings ordering note on top of the
applied anti-cannibalization delta.

1. Classic fallback published without any cannibalization check: when the keyword
   queue is empty, processarCategoriaComFila delegates to the classic
   processarCategoria, which published straight to persistGeneratedPost with no
   checkpoint. Added Checkpoint 2 (verificarCanibalizacao, L1 lexical + L2
   semantic) right before that persist, same treatment (rejected + reason),
   fail-open. This is the very path that produced today's cannibalized posts.

2. Embeddings fetch had no timeout: a hung provider connection would only die on
   Node's ~5min default while holding the category advisory lock. Added
   AbortSignal.timeout(15s) per attempt; the error falls into the existing
   retry/backoff which returns null (degrades to lexical) fast.

3. Embeddings provider precedence inverted: the Replit OpenAI proxy does NOT
   route the embeddings API (documented as unsupported), so trying it first was
   always-fails-first. Now own key (voyage / BLOG_EMBEDDING_API_KEY) is tried
   first; the Replit proxy is the last resort and logs a one-time WARN.

Typecheck + build pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013R8r3kYmmxtUVyMSRh4xk1
